{
  "id": "28116_ketsuisuru",
  "headword": "{決意|けつい}する",
  "reading": "けついする",
  "romaji": "ketsuisuru",
  "part_of_speech": "suru verb",
  "gloss": "to resolve; to make up one's mind",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to resolve; to make up one's mind; to be determined",
      "explanation": "To firmly decide to do something, with strong determination. Weightier and more deliberate than {決|き}める, implying a considered, serious commitment."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "28116_ketsuisuru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{留学|りゅうがく}を{決意|けつい}する。",
      "english": "I resolve to study abroad.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28116_ketsuisuru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{彼|かれ}は{独立|どくりつ}を{決意|けつい}した。",
      "english": "He made up his mind to become independent.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28116_ketsuisuru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{何度|なんど}も{悩|なや}んだ{末|すえ}に、{会社|かいしゃ}を{辞|や}めることを{決意|けつい}した。",
      "english": "After agonizing many times, I resolved to quit the company.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "{決意|けつい}する is a transitive suru-verb expressing a firm, weighty decision. The thing decided is marked with を, or a clause + ことを.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {辞職|じしょく}を{決意|けつい}する: to resolve to resign\n- 〜することを{決意|けつい}する: to make up one's mind to do ~\n- {固|かた}く{決意|けつい}する: to be firmly resolved\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {決|き}める: to decide — everyday and lighter, for choices large and small\n- {決断|けつだん}する: to make a (difficult) decision — emphasizes choosing between options",
